# Every variable the app reads. All optional: leave them empty and the app still runs, with
# sign-in and Turnstile off. Names and rules are checked in src/lib/env-schema.ts; a half-set
# pair fails fast with the variable's name (never its value).
#
# Local dev: copy to .env (never commit the copy). Production: build-time values are set in the
# build's environment; secrets are Worker secrets, e.g. `pnpm exec wrangler secret put CLERK_SECRET_KEY`.

# --- Build time (public, baked into the HTML) ---
# The production origin, no trailing slash. Feeds canonicals, og:url, sitemap, robots, security.txt.
# Unset: canonicals use http://localhost:3000 and every non-localhost host is sent noindex.
SITE_URL=
# Where to report a security problem (security.txt). Default: mailto:security@<SITE_URL host>.
SECURITY_CONTACT=

# --- Runtime (Worker vars and secrets) ---
# Clerk sign-in. Set both or neither. `clerk env pull` writes both names as they are here (Clerk's
# TanStack Start name). The publishable key is public and read at runtime despite the VITE_ prefix.
# The old name CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY still works, with a warning in the Worker log: rename it.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional: Clerk's JWKS public key (PEM), so bearer tokens on /api/v1 are verified without a call to Clerk.
CLERK_JWT_KEY=
# Optional: more origins a Clerk session token may come from (its azp claim), comma-separated exact
# origins, no wildcards. Already allowed with nothing set: SITE_URL, localhost in local builds, and
# in test builds the test Worker's workers.dev URL and its pr-<n> previews. Production with Clerk keys
# refuses to start unless SITE_URL or this is set. A token without azp is refused (Clerk's rule).
CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=
# Optional, "true" or "false" (default): a native app (the monorepo-expo pack's mobile app) sends no
# Origin, so its tokens have no azp. "true" lets such a bearer token through on /api/v1 only, and only
# with an `app` claim equal to CLERK_NATIVE_APP_CLAIM; the cookie and any token that names a wrong
# origin are still refused. Any other native app on the same Clerk instance can use its tokens (the
# claim is in every token the instance issues): use one Clerk instance per product.
CLERK_ALLOW_NATIVE_TOKENS=
# With native tokens on: the value of the `app` claim you add in Clerk (Sessions -> Customize session
# token: {"app": "<this value>"}), e.g. the repo name. Lowercase, 1 to 64 of a-z 0-9 . _ -. Not a
# secret. Unset: every native token is refused (Worker log: clerk_native_claim_missing).
CLERK_NATIVE_APP_CLAIM=
# Cloudflare Turnstile on forms that opt in. Set both or neither. Test keys: see the stack skill.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Not here: wrangler.jsonc vars per environment ---
# LAUNCHED ("true" or "false": the "Coming soon" page) and SITE_PROTECTION (access, password or none)
# live in each environment's "vars" in wrangler.jsonc. SITE_PASSWORD, for the password gate on the
# test site only, is made and set by `node scripts/setup-cloudflare.mjs --protect password`.
# With Cloudflare Access, setup-cloudflare also writes ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN, ACCESS_AUD and (production
# paths only) ACCESS_PATHS into that environment's vars: the Worker checks Access's JWT with them.
#
# --- Not here either: .env.cloudflare.local (git-ignored), read only by setup-cloudflare ---
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_TOKEN, and each Access login's OAuth client:
# ACCESS_<LOGIN>_CLIENT_ID and ACCESS_<LOGIN>_CLIENT_SECRET for GOOGLE, GITHUB, FACEBOOK, LINKEDIN,
# YANDEX, ENTRA (+ ACCESS_ENTRA_TENANT_ID) or OIDC (+ ACCESS_OIDC_AUTH_URL, _TOKEN_URL, _CERTS_URL).
